  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 354 AM EDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\n- Showers and storms possible this afternoon through Saturday\n\nSmall chances for showers and thunderstorms exist this afternoon\nand early evening to the southeast of Grand Rapids. Areas from\nKalamazoo to Lansing and Jackson stand the best chances to see\nthis activity but it is not certain. The HREF does not have a good\nhandle of convective chances today. The HRRR and other high\nresolution models seem to be picking up on a signal for this area\nwhere MUCAPE values may exceed 1500 j/kg. If storms develop not\nexpecting severe weather given low shear and only modest\ninstability. \n\nTonight there is a threat that some stronger storms may try to\nadvect in from the west overnight along and ahead of a cold front.\nMachine learning schemes are not bullish on severe weather today\nor tonight though and the SPC only has our area in a general \nthunder outlook. Shear remains weak tonight.\n\n\n- Storms possible Sunday into Monday  \n\nA better chance at some stronger storms looks to occur in the\nSunday into Monday time frame as a warm front sets up to our\nsouthwest. This is when surface dew points (around 70) and PWAT \nvalues (1.75 to 2.00 inches) peak in the 7 day forecast. Embedded\nshortwaves in a generally zonal upper flow will likely aid in\nthunderstorm initiation and maintenance. A 25-35 knot low level\njet will also aid storms. MUCAPE values will push towards or\npotentially exceed 2000 j/kg. Sunday night and Monday will likely\nbe the best chance at storms. SPC maintains a general thunder\noutlook for us on Sunday and Monday as well. \n\n- Trending slightly cooler and drier into mid next week\n\nWe trend a bit cooler into mid week as 850mb temperatures cool\nslightly from the upper teens (Sunday night) to the lower teens by\nThursday. GFS MOS guidance has highs back into the 70s at GRR on\nThursday. The surface pattern looks fairly diffuse Tuesday into\nWednesday which will trend towards ridging by Thursday.\n\nOverall the focus of the entire 7 day forecast is on periodic\nthunderstorm chances. Some locally heavy rain will be possible,\nespecially from Sunday into Monday.",
